h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 878)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Drop it.</b> Drop the delivery folder, one of its files, or a zip onto the Source Links window and every clip is found nearby &#8212; the folder, its parent, its grandparent &#8212; and linked. Drop a zip onto the main window and it is unpacked and sorted through: a session package inside opens as that session, an invite is offered, a session file opens, media joins, and the review&#8217;s missing clips relink from it.</li>
<li><b>Export Session Package: Zip the package</b> (one file to send) and <b>Deliver to</b> &#8212; Suite (into the job&#8217;s 10_DELIVERIES, watched until Suite has uploaded it), Google Drive, Dropbox or Box (the synced folder; a share link is made when rclone knows the service). The clips&#8217; source links and the invite&#8217;s note then say where the originals are.</li>
<li>The Source Links window follows the playlist as it changes.</li>
<li>The host sees what each person did about the media under their name &#8212; &#8220;fetched from delivery.zip&#8221;, &#8220;couldn&#8217;t fetch: access denied&#8221; &#8212; and a missing clip&#8217;s marker says why.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
